{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
May [C]Your sal[Cmaj7]vation, oh [C]God, set us se[Am]curely [A5/E]on [Am]high
For [C]You have [Cmaj7]heard the [C]needy, You have heard our [Am]cry [A5/E] [Am]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
You who seek the [Dm]Lord, [G]let your heart re[Am]vive [A5/E] [Am]
(Let your heart revive)
And praise the [Dm]name of [G]Jesus with [Am]song
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
For [C]God will [Cmaj7]save [C]Zion and build the [Am]cities [A5/E]of [Am]Judah
And [C]those who [Cmaj7]love Your [C]name will dwell in [Am]it [A5/E] [Am]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
For [Dm]God has said, “[G]This is my resting [Am]place for[C]ever;
[Dm]Here I will dwell, for [G]I have desired [A]it”
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]We will [Cmaj7]magnify [C]Him with thanks[Am]giving [A5/E] [Am]
And [C]it will [Cmaj7]please the [C]Lord more than sacri[Am]fice [A5/E] [Am]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
You who seek the [Dm]Lord, [G]let your heart re[Am]vive [A5/E] [Am]
(Let your heart revive)
And praise the [Dm]name of [G]Jesus with [A]song
